IMPORT prelude

-- Wills Act 1968 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. Dates are compared by serial.
--
-- READINGS (forks F1-F3 in NOTES.md):
--   "a period of N months commencing on the day" (s 12A (3), (4), (5) (b)) includes that day: it ends on the day before
--   the same date N months on, or, where the later month has no such date, on that month's last day.
--   "a period of N has elapsed since the day" (s 12A (5) (a), (b) (ii)) excludes that day: the period ends on the same
--   date a month on (or the month's last day), or on the 7th day after; it "has elapsed" from the next day.
--   "survive ... by 30 days" / "for a period of 30 days" (ss 31, 31B, 31C) excludes the day of death: the 30 days are
--   the 30 days after it, and a person survives them if alive at the end of the 30th day.
-- No date is moved for a weekend or a public holiday (the Legislation Act 2001 is not deposited).
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Wills Act 1968 (ACT)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a number of plain days after a day (before it, if the number is negative).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

-- The same date n months on (n from 1 to 12); where the later month has no such date, that month's last day. The
-- boolean says whether the same date exists.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the same date exists` n `months after` `the day` IF
    DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the days in month` (`the month n months after` n `the day`) (`the year n months after` n `the day`)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month n months after` n `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS n GREATER THAN 12
    THEN DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS n MINUS 12
    ELSE DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year n months after` n `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS n GREATER THAN 12
    THEN DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day`

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` `the month` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`the month` PLUS 1) `the year`) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the day` MEANS
    IF `the same date exists` n `months after` `the day`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) `the month` `the year`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the days in month` `the month` `the year`) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the month` MEANS `the month n months after` n `the day`
        `the year` MEANS `the year n months after` n `the day`

-- Fork F1: the last day of "a period of n months commencing on" a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `months commencing on` `the day` MEANS
    IF `the same date exists` n `months after` `the day`
    THEN `the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (`the date` n `months after` `the day`)
    ELSE `the date` n `months after` `the day`

-- Fork F2: the first day on which "a period of n months has elapsed since" a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day after` n `months have elapsed since` `the day` MEANS
    `the date` 1 `days after` (`the date` n `months after` `the day`)

-- Fork F3: whether a person who died on a day survived another's death by 30 days.
GIVEN `the person's death` IS A DATE, `the other's death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person who died on` `the person's death` `survived the death on` `the other's death` `by 30 days` IF
    `the days from` `the other's death` `to` `the person's death` GREATER THAN 30
